%LC理
\dEh?\d%K%P
「诶？」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dThe moon really is red.\d%K%P
「月亮果然是红的啊」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dY-Yeah...\d%K%P
「啊，是啊…」%K%P
It was an obvious attempt at changing the topic to lighten\nmy mood.%K%P
她这明显是注意到了我的心思，\n故意来转换一下话题吧…%K%P
It was so obvious that even I could tell... which suddenly\nfilled me with happiness.%K%P
所以，她故意将对我的在意表现得让我都能看出来，\n这让我感到很开心。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
Glancing at the sky, I saw a measly amount of stars -- as\none would expect from a large metropolis.%K%P
抬头仰望，\n这片与大都市相得益彰的星空虽说闪耀，\n却让我觉着有些无聊。%K%P
Our conversation came to an end, but the mood remained\nwarm as we both enjoyed the slow passage of time.%K%P
对话虽然中断了，但我们也没有感到什么异样，\n只是静静享受着这慢慢流逝的时间。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dOn days when Mom came home early, I'd always go outside\nand watch the moon and the stars like this while waiting\nfor her.\d%K%P
「在妈妈回来的还比较早的那段日子，\n我总是会坐在这里，像现在这样看着星星和月亮」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...That's pretty lax behavior for a kid.\d%K%P
「…真是不雅的举止啊」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dHmph.\d%K%P
「啰嗦！」%K%P
Mitoko gave me an indignant look for pointing out another\nunpleasant detail, but she seemed a touch less\nintimidating this time.%K%P
即便如此，瞪着因得意忘形而又斤斤计较起来的我，\n美都子这次露出了笑容。%K%P
Dangling her legs from the fence of the Terrace House\nHinosaka, Mitoko was now at the same height as me.%K%P
Terrace House阳之坂有着围墙，\n她坐在这高高混凝土围墙上摇晃着双脚，\n与平常不同的是，她现在比我的视线要高了。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dHow was your first day?\d%K%P
「第一天上班感觉怎样？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI guess you could say it was a little exhausting.\d%K%P
「果然是有点累吧？」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dWhat did you do? If it's sales, were you, like, going\naround and greeting all your business partners or\nsomething?\d%K%P
「做了些什么啊都？\n做营业的话，是忙着跟顾客问候？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dThat's not something you do on your first day. I just\nread a bunch of their documents and learned about the\ncompany. Then I answered the phone a few times.\d%K%P
